 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**For today, no need to decide whether to skip:** it’s **Sunday, October 18, 2026, in Kuala Lumpur**, so regular KL schools are not in session. If your children have a special class today, check with that school. ([moe.gov.my](https://www.moe.gov.my/storage/files/shares/Takwim/Takwim%20Persekolahan/Kalendar%20Akademik%202026.pdf))\n\nThe haze still calls for care: a Department of Environment–sourced reading for Cheras was **162 (unhealthy) at midnight**. Keep the kids’ outdoor activity to a minimum, especially if either has asthma or breathing symptoms. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuala-lumpur))\n\nFor **Monday**, check the official APIMS reading near the school and the school’s notice before leaving. The Education Ministry’s latest stated rule is to close schools when Malaysia’s **API reaches 200** and stop outdoor school activities when it exceeds **100**. It also says parents concerned about a child’s health may keep them home **if they notify the school**. ([bernama.com](https://www.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854))",
